<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-110096 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/LEGOLAND-Florida-Pirate-Island-Hotel-Features-Amenities.jpg" alt="" width="1177" height="495" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/LEGOLAND-Florida-Pirate-Island-Hotel-Features-Amenities.jpg 1177w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/LEGOLAND-Florida-Pirate-Island-Hotel-Features-Amenities-300x126.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/LEGOLAND-Florida-Pirate-Island-Hotel-Features-Amenities-1024x431.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/LEGOLAND-Florida-Pirate-Island-Hotel-Features-Amenities-768x323.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1177px) 100vw, 1177px" /></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Difference Between LEGOLAND Resorts and LEGOLAND Discovery Centers – Final Thoughts</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Both offer premium entertainment for kids aged between 2 and 12, but they do so differently. While the resorts focus on the outdoor/indoor rides and attractions, the discovery centers are completely indoor.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For my recommendation, pick the discovery centers if you only have a few minutes to spare, maybe after work. But if you have an entire weekend or two to three days to spare, the LEGOLAND resorts offer a better deal.</span></p>
